+### Embedded documents (cards)
+
+A host page can embed its own documents in a board: a **card** is a rectangle whose box carries an `embed` field naming one of the
+host's documents. The host draws the document's content over the card (an overlay above the canvas) and edits it there; the board
+keeps the card a box like any other (select, move, resize, copy, delete, undo), draws its frame, its shadow and its label, and tells
+the host where the cards are. The native format gains one optional field, so its version stays 2:
+
+```json
+{ "id": "k3j2h1g0f9", "kind": { "type": "box", "geom": "rect", "frame": { "x": -240.0, "y": -180.0, "w": 480.0, "h": 360.0 },
+    "label": { "text": [ { "text": "Meeting notes", "bold": true, "color": "#1d2430" } ], "family": "sans", "size": 24.0, "align": "center" },
+    "embed": { "item": "0192f0e0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001" } },
+  "style": { "stroke": "#c4cad4", "fill": "#ffffff", "width": 1.0, "dash": "solid", "opacity": 1.0, "roundness": 0.04, "shadow": true },
+  "layer": "main" }
+```
+
+- Only a `rect` box whose `embed` is an object with a string `item` is a card; `item` is the host's business (the engine never reads
+  it). The label is the document's title as last saved: what exports, previews and other readers show. Fields of `embed` other than
+  `item` are not kept, and a value that is not such an object loads as a plain box (it is dropped on the next save), so a board written
+  by another program always opens. A box kind with the key `embed` twice cannot be read (as any other repeated field).
+- Without a host page (the page of its own, the desktop application) a card is a plain rectangle: its label is edited as any other.
+
+`mount` takes three more callbacks, called after the frame like the others; points and rectangles are in CSS pixels of the canvas
+(top left 0, 0), frames in world units:
+
+| Callback | When |
+|---|---|
+| `onEmbedLayout({page, zoom, originX, originY, canvas, occluders, embeds, items, clipboard, editing})` | after a frame in which any of it changed, at most once per frame: the current page, the camera (`screen = origin + world × zoom`), the drawing area, the engine's own interface over it (`occluders`: floating cards, menus, popups, tooltips, toasts, windows), the cards of the current page on visible layers in drawing order (`{id, item, x, y, w, h, angle, label, selected, locked}`, as drawn, gestures included), every distinct `item` of the board, sorted, every distinct `item` of the cards on the board's clipboard (cut or copied, so still to be pasted, here or on the next board), sorted, and the card being edited by the host. A page without cards reports no pan or zoom. |
+| `onEmbedOpen({id, item, point})` | instead of editing a card's label (double-click, Enter, the menu's "Edit text"); `point` is the double-click, `null` otherwise. Never on a read-only board |
+| `onEmbedEditEnd({id, reason})` | the editing set by `setEmbedEditing` ended in the board: `'press'` (a primary or secondary press anywhere in the board), `'focus'` (the board took the keyboard focus, other than by a press of the middle button, which pans), `'gone'` (the card left the current page, or `setBoard`) |
+
+| Call | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| `insertEmbed({item, title, at, w?, h?})` → id or `null` | adds a card centred on `at` (`'center'`: the centre of the view, or a canvas point), `w` × `h` world units (480 × 360 by default), labelled `title` in bold, on the first visible and unlocked layer: one undo step, selected; `null` on a read-only board. A label being typed is validated first |
+| `setEmbedEditing(id \| null)` | the host edits that card: it stays selected without handles, the board handles no key and hides its style panel, and the first primary or secondary press in the board or the board taking the focus ends it (`onEmbedEditEnd`); a primary press that ends it does nothing else on the canvas, and the middle button still pans. An id that is not a card of the current page is ignored; `null` ends it without an event |
+| `setEmbedTitles({item: title, …})` | the documents' live titles: shown as the cards' labels at once, with no undo step and no revision (a title change alone never makes the board dirty); the next save keeps them. `setBoard` forgets them |
+| `requestEmbedLayout()` | `onEmbedLayout` after the next frame even when nothing changed |
+
+A single card has no rotation handle while hosted (the host draws the document upright), and the style panel has no text settings for a
+selection of cards alone (their label is only the title). The wheel's Shift and Alt are read from the wheel event itself: the board learns
+the other modifiers from key events on its canvas, which it does not get while the host page has the keyboard focus.
+
